{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43341010",
      "title": "Controlling the Image Size",
      "lectureOrder": 196,
      "videoOrder": 182,
      "sourceHash": "502211bf54ea6cfdbb2cd519395db3db8d15a95bdb51a90b1bde76eda29792d3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 3,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmüller] So this next image component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "automatically determines the width and height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 7.56,
          "en": "of the input file when you're using it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.56,
          "end": 10.02,
          "en": "And therefore you should indeed make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.02,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "that the input file isn't unnecessarily large",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 17.73,
          "en": "because otherwise, even though NextJS will perform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.73,
          "end": 21.342,
          "en": "some resizing for different screen sizes automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.342,
          "end": 25.35,
          "en": "or for different screen resolutions specifically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 27.06,
          "en": "even though NextJS will do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.06,
          "end": 29.46,
          "en": "if the raw input file is too big,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.46,
          "end": 32.91,
          "en": "of course the entire base for the resizing operations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.91,
          "end": 35.193,
          "en": "performed by NextJS will be wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 38.13,
          "en": "So one thing you could do then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.13,
          "end": 42.51,
          "en": "and you should typically do is resize that input image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.51,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "But one other thing you could do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 49.08,
          "en": "is manually override the inferred width and height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.08,
          "end": 51.03,
          "en": "And you can do this by setting the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.03,
          "end": 54.573,
          "en": "and height props on that NextJS image component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "And here I could, for example, set that to 100 each,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 64.16,
          "en": "so to 100 pixels each and of course you should set a width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.59,
          "end": 68.94,
          "en": "and height that's in line to the approximate size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.94,
          "end": 71.22,
          "en": "at which the image will be displayed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.22,
          "end": 74.163,
          "en": "So that comes down to your specific use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 77.34,
          "en": "But I can set the width and height like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.34,
          "end": 81.09,
          "en": "and if I then save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.09,
          "end": 82.17,
          "en": "you will see that of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.17,
          "end": 84.42,
          "en": "still the image element is rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.42,
          "end": 88.59,
          "en": "but now my width and height has been set as a value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.59,
          "end": 93.06,
          "en": "on that image element and the sizes that are generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.06,
          "end": 96.15,
          "en": "by NextJS automatically, you can tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.15,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "the generated width here by this special query parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 102.21000000000001,
          "en": "that's set on these image URLs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "These sizes got down and were decreased",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 110.22,
          "en": "and therefore now by manually setting a lower width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.22,
          "end": 113.43,
          "en": "and height than the input image has,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.43,
          "end": 116.64,
          "en": "I'm making sure that NextJS actually serves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.64,
          "end": 118.923,
          "en": "smaller image files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 124.76,
          "en": "Now whilst you can tweak the width and height like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.04,
          "end": 127.26,
          "en": "this is actually not the recommended way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.26,
          "end": 129.66,
          "en": "though I will say it does work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.66,
          "end": 133.02,
          "en": "and it therefore can be a decent workaround",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 137.853,
          "en": "or a quick way of getting NextJS to resize an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.87,
          "end": 141.27,
          "en": "Still, when importing a local image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.27,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "it's typically not recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 146.28,
          "en": "to set the width and height like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.28,
          "end": 150.84,
          "en": "Instead, you should keep it to the native raw sizes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.84,
          "end": 153.54,
          "en": "the raw width and height of the input file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.54,
          "end": 156.51,
          "en": "and instead, if you want to resize the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.51,
          "end": 160.77,
          "en": "it's recommended that you do this with the sizes prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.77,
          "end": 164.043,
          "en": "which is another prop you can add on that image element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.39,
          "end": 168.39,
          "en": "And the sizes prop then can take",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.39,
          "end": 171.39,
          "en": "actually a list of different sizes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.39,
          "end": 175.14,
          "en": "The image should assume depending on the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 177.84,
          "en": "of the view port so that you could set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.84,
          "end": 180.72,
          "en": "a responsive image but if like here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.72,
          "end": 184.02,
          "en": "we have one size that's used all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.02,
          "end": 189.02,
          "en": "this image size doesn't change as my viewport width changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.39,
          "end": 192.87,
          "en": "if that's the case, you can just set up one value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.87,
          "end": 195.78,
          "en": "for this sizes setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.78,
          "end": 199.29,
          "en": "and that value could be 10vw, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.29,
          "end": 201.51,
          "en": "which is a CSS unit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.51,
          "end": 203.91,
          "en": "And this means that this image will take up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.91,
          "end": 208.413,
          "en": "approximately 10% of the available viewport.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.88,
          "end": 212.88,
          "en": "And this setting will then also get NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.88,
          "end": 217.23,
          "en": "to resize the image and serve an image of a different size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.23,
          "end": 218.433,
          "en": "behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "So that's an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 225.99,
          "en": "and actually the recommended way of resizing an image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.99,
          "end": 228.18,
          "en": "and you can therefore also learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.18,
          "end": 230.85,
          "en": "about using this sizes prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.85,
          "end": 233.85,
          "en": "in the official NextJS documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.85,
          "end": 237.72,
          "en": "However, I will say that for use cases like this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.72,
          "end": 240.75,
          "en": "where I have a fixed size image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.75,
          "end": 243.84,
          "en": "where I don't need different resizing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.84,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "for different viewport widths,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.42,
          "end": 251.31,
          "en": "I personally actually like to manually override the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.31,
          "end": 254.37,
          "en": "and height of the raw input file and set a width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.37,
          "end": 257.37,
          "en": "and height explicitly as I'm doing it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.37,
          "end": 260.94,
          "en": "to get NextJS to serve me a different image file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.94,
          "end": 264.78,
          "en": "of a different size, simply because that's a quick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.78,
          "end": 266.52,
          "en": "and easy solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.52,
          "end": 270.84,
          "en": "Nonetheless, you should know about this sizes prop as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.84,
          "end": 273.24,
          "en": "Of course, as mentioned, it would be even better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 273.24,
          "end": 275.668,
          "en": "to decrease the size of the input image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.668,
          "end": 279.12,
          "en": "but manually setting a width and height that differs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.12,
          "end": 283.08299999999997,
          "en": "from the base image size also can be an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
